Date: Thu, 21 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] core/storage: cap Pillow decompression (anti-bomb DoS)

make_thumbnail() opened user-supplied image bytes with no pixel-count bound,
so a crafted image (tiny on disk, enormous decompressed bitmap) could exhaust
worker memory before thumbnail() ever ran. Enforce a conservative
MAX_IMAGE_PIXELS cap and let Pillow raise DecompressionBombError (caught by
the existing except) instead of allocating gigabytes.

Refs: docs/SECURITY.md finding 1, THREAT-MODEL.md T11.

---
 app/core/storage.py | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/app/core/storage.py b/app/core/storage.py
--- a/app/core/storage.py
+++ b/app/core/storage.py
@@
     """Generate a JPEG thumbnail in-memory (Pillow). Returns None for
     non-image inputs (video files, unknown types)."""
     try:
         from PIL import Image  # local import keeps Pillow optional at module load
+        # Anti decompression-bomb (THREAT-MODEL T11): bound the total pixel
+        # count a user-supplied image may expand to before we downscale it.
+        # Pillow raises DecompressionBombError past this limit, which the
+        # outer `except Exception` turns into a "no thumbnail" result.
+        try:
+            Image.MAX_IMAGE_PIXELS = 200_000_000  # ~200 MP hard cap
+        except Exception:
+            pass
     except Exception:
         return None
     try:
         img = Image.open(io.BytesIO(image_bytes))
